{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/Appearance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The table follows the system look by default: system fonts and colors,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"alternating row backgrounds, a rounded selection like the Finder sidebar,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"overlay scrollers, light and dark mode, the user’s accent color, and a Liquid"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Glass summary bar on macOS 26 (a header material on earlier systems). Rows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scroll underneath the summary bar."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Sizes","text":"Sizes","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Property","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Default","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowHeight","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"24","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The rows’ height, unless the delegate gives rows their own (","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableViewRowHeights","isActive":true},{"text":") or a column wraps text (then the height of a row of one line).","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/headerRowHeight","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"28","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The column titles.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/groupHeaderHeight","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"24","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The group band, only shown when there are groups.","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/summaryRowHeight","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"30","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The summary row.","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"anchor":"Fonts-colors-and-density","text":"Fonts, colors and density","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The table uses the system fonts and colors, following light and dark mode,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"accent color and contrast settings. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/tableStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" changes them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where an app needs its own look; anything left "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" stays the system’s:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["table.tableStyle = GHTableStyle(","    fontSize: 15,                      \/\/ cells and the summary row","    headerFontSize: 12,                \/\/ column titles","    textColor: .labelColor,","    backgroundColor: NSColor(named: \"TableBackground\"),","    stripeColors: [.clear, NSColor(named: \"Stripe\")!],","    groupRowColor: NSColor(named: \"GroupRow\"))","table.density = .compact               \/\/ or .regular (24 points), .spacious"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/density"},{"type":"text","text":" sets "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowHeight"},{"type":"text","text":" for the style’s font,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with a little, some or more room around the text, like Finder’s list sizes;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it follows a later font size change. Give the style the same color objects"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each time (the renderer resolves each color once per appearance)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Rows-and-selection","text":"Rows and selection","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/usesAlternatingRowBackgroundColors","type":"reference"},{"text":" stripes the rows with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s alternating content colors.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/showsVerticalGridLines","type":"reference"},{"text":" draws thin lines between columns.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/selectionHighlightStyle","type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".rounded"},{"text":" (inset, rounded","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"corners, like macOS lists; the table then keeps a small margin at its edges)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".fullWidth"},{"text":" (a plain band across the whole row, like classic tables).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The selection is shown in the accent color while the table is focused and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in gray otherwise.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Highlighting-rows-by-their-data","text":"Highlighting rows by their data","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The delegate can tint a row’s background and put a colored marker at its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"leading edge, for example green for profitable campaigns and red for losing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ones:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["\/\/ Created once: the table asks for every visible row while scrolling.","static let profitTint = NSColor.systemGreen.withAlphaComponent(0.10)","static let lossTint = NSColor.systemRed.withAlphaComponent(0.10)","","func tableView(_ tableView: GHTableView, backgroundColorForRow row: Int) -> NSColor? {","    let roi = data.campaigns[row].roi","    return roi > 0 ? Self.profitTint : roi < 0 ? Self.lossTint : nil","}","","func tableView(_ tableView: GHTableView, markerColorForRow row: Int) -> NSColor? {","    data.campaigns[row].isOverBudget ? .systemOrange : nil","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use light, translucent tints so text stays readable, and return the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"color objects every time (static constants): the table compares them to skip","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unchanged rows.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Tints replace the alternating stripes of their rows. Selected rows show the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"selection instead of the tint, and keep the marker.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"System colors like ","type":"text"},{"code":"systemGreen","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" adapt to dark mode and accent changes by","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"themselves.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The table asks when rows come into view and on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/reloadData()","isActive":true},{"text":". If the condition behind a tint changes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without a data change, call ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reloadData()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"text":"Empty state","anchor":"Empty-state","type":"heading","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"While there are no rows, the table shows ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/emptyStateText","type":"reference"},{"text":", or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"your own ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/emptyStateView","type":"reference"},{"text":" (for example with a button to create","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the first record). The table places it; the app says what it is.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Without any data (the data source has no rows), the table shows only the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"empty state, centered: no header, row stripes or summary row.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowFilter"},{"text":" hides every row, the columns stay and the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"empty state shows in the rows area. See ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/FilteringAndSearch"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"While the data updates (see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/isUpdatingData","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":"), the spinner","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"takes its place, and it comes back if there are still no rows. There’s no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"need to clear the text while loading.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"anchor":"Scrolling","text":"Scrolling","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The table scrolls by itself, like a scroll view:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"trackpads scroll with momentum and bounce at the top and bottom; turn the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bounce off with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/bouncesVertically","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":";","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"gestures lock to the axis they start on, so vertical scrolling doesn’t drift","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sideways;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"overlay scrollers appear while scrolling and expand under the pointer;","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with “Show scroll bars: Always” in System Settings, the table shows classic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scrollers that take up space;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"clicking the scroller track pages, and holding it keeps paging;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"scrolling on an axis the table has nothing to scroll on goes to the view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that contains it, like a nested scroll view’s: a table of a few rows in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"form scrolls the form (alone in a window, its rows still bounce).","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In code, read ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/contentOffset","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and scroll with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/scroll(to:)"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/scrollRowToVisible(_:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/didScrollNotification"},{"text":" tells every change of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/contentOffset"},{"text":" once the rows are laid out there, where","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"NSTableView apps watch the clip view’s bounds: for example, load the next","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"page when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rowIndexes(in: table.bounds)"},{"text":" reaches the last rows.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/willStartLiveScrollNotification","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/didLiveScrollNotification"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/didEndLiveScrollNotification"},{"text":" follow the user’s scrolling","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"like a scroll view’s: a trackpad gesture or a drag of the overlay scroller,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ending with its momentum. Never make","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the table the document of an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSScrollView"},{"text":" (a form around it in one is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fine).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Localization","anchor":"Localization","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The table’s own texts — its menus (the summary scope, columns, grouping,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"views), the column filter and save view dialogs, Undo names and what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"VoiceOver reads — are localized in English and Russian; the summary scope","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"titles can be replaced with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/summaryScopeTitles","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". Everything","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"else the user reads — column","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"titles, tool tips, menus, empty state texts, tags and mark labels — comes from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"your app, localized as you like. Numbers and dates are formatted in the user’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"locale.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Right-to-left languages","type":"heading","anchor":"Right-to-left-languages"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a right-to-left interface (Arabic, Hebrew; the table follows"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/userInterfaceLayoutDirection","type":"reference"},{"text":", which AppKit sets from the app’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"language) the whole table is mirrored, like AppKit’s own controls:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The first column is at the right; leading frozen columns stay at the right"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge and trailing ones at the left; the vertical scroller is at the left."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each cell’s content is mirrored within it: leading text at the right,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"numbers aligned to the trailing side (the left), tags listed from the right,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data bars growing from the right, outline and group indents and their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disclosure triangles at the right, the triangles of collapsed rows pointing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"left. Text itself reads as written: every line moves whole, so Arabic,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Hebrew and mixed text keep their order."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Column titles put the filter button and the sort arrow at their left;"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"columns resize from their left edge and move by dragging the other way."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Left Arrow goes to the next column and Right Arrow back (on group headers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and tree rows, Right Arrow collapses and Left Arrow expands); Tab still goes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to the next column. Swiping a row to the right shows its trailing actions,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at the left."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/contentOffset"},{"type":"text","text":" still counts from the leading end: 0 shows the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first columns, at the right. Printing and PDF put the first column at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right too."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Set ","type":"text"},{"code":"userInterfaceLayoutDirection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" yourself to show one table mirrored or not,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever the app’s language.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham"]]},"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Gingham"}],"title":"Appearance"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Appearance and Behavior","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/KeyboardAndAccessibility","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHSelectionHighlightStyle","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableStyle","doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableDensity"],"anchor":"Appearance-and-Behavior"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/gingham\/appearance"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"Adjust sizes, highlight rows by their data, and choose how selection and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"scrolling look.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/bouncesVertically":{"title":"bouncesVertically","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"bouncesVertically"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/bouncesVertically","url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/ghtableview\/bouncesvertically","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Elastic overscroll (“bounce”) at the top and bottom edges with trackpads,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"like system scroll views. Mouse wheels never bounce."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A fast table for business data on the Mac, iPad and iPhone: frozen columns,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"column groups, a summary row with formulas, row grouping with subtotals, search and filters, stable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selection across reloads, and live updates."}],"type":"topic","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/gingham","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham","title":"Gingham"},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/summaryRowHeight":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/summaryRowHeight","type":"topic","title":"summaryRowHeight","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"summaryRowHeight"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14CoreFoundation7CGFloatV","text":"CGFloat"}],"url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/ghtableview\/summaryrowheight","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Height of the summary row."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/contentOffset":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"contentOffset"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:@S@CGPoint","text":"CGPoint"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/contentOffset","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Scroll position: x within the scrolling columns, y within the rows."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/ghtableview\/contentoffset","title":"contentOffset","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/rowFilter":{"kind":"symbol","title":"rowFilter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Rows shown, e.g. for a search field. Row indexes in the API (selection,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delegate and data source calls) stay data source indexes; summaries,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selection, copying and VoiceOver only cover the rows shown. When the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"data changes, call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reloadData()"},{"type":"text","text":" (it filters again), or a targeted"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"update (it filters the changed rows again; the other rows keep their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match); set the filter again when only the condition behind"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isIncluded"},{"type":"text","text":" changed. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isIncluded"},{"type":"text","text":" is kept by the table: capture"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"self"},{"type":"text","text":" weakly in it. The first search of a large table reads its words"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the background (see "},{"code":"synchronousSearchLimit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/rowFilter","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/ghtableview\/rowfilter","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"rowFilter","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"text":"GHRowFilter","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Gingham11GHRowFilterV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/FilteringAndSearch":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/FilteringAndSearch","title":"Filtering and Search","kind":"article","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/filteringandsearch","abstract":[{"text":"Show only some rows, for a search field or switches like “active only”, while","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the data source keeps all of them.","type":"text"}]},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/willStartLiveScrollNotification":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"willStartLiveScrollNotification"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation12NotificationV","text":"Notification"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation12NotificationV4Namea","text":"Name"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/willStartLiveScrollNotification","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Posted when the user starts scrolling the table with a gesture or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its scroller, like "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSScrollView.willStartLiveScrollNotification"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/gingham\/ghtableview\/willstartlivescrollnotification","title":"willStartLiveScrollNotification","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://ngtable.Gingham/documentation/Gingham/GHTableView/scroll(to:)":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\